.TH QDBG 1 "2026 October 31" "Qore 3.0" "Qore Programming Language"
.SH NAME
qdbg \- interactive debugger for Qore programs
.br
qdbg-remote \- remote debugger client for Qore
.br
qdbg-server \- debug server for remote Qore debugging
.br
qdbg-vsc-adapter \- VS Code Debug Adapter Protocol bridge
.br
qdbg-mcp \- MCP server that lets coding agents debug Qore programs
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B qdbg
[\fIoptions\fP] \fIprogram\fP [\fIprogram-args\fP]...
.PP
.B qdbg-remote
[\fIoptions\fP] \fIurl\fP|\fIconnection\fP[/\fIpath\fP]
.PP
.B qdbg-server
[\fIoptions\fP] \fIprogram\fP [\fIprogram-args\fP]...
.PP
.B qdbg-vsc-adapter
[\fIoptions\fP]
.PP
.B qdbg-mcp
[\fIoptions\fP]
.SH DESCRIPTION
The \fBqdbg\fR family provides debugging support for Qore programs.
.SS qdbg
Interactive local debugger with command-line editing via linenoise.
Supports breakpoints, stepping, variable inspection, and session
save/restore.
When its input is not a terminal, \fBqdbg\fR runs a script of commands:
the first command is processed when the program has attached to the
debugger, and a command that resumes a thread returns when the thread
stops again or stops being debugged, so that each command is processed at
the stop that it is written for.
.SS qdbg-remote
Connects to a running \fBqdbg-server\fR instance via WebSocket for
remote debugging.
.SS qdbg-server
HTTP server providing a WebSocket debug endpoint.
Run the target program under this server, then attach with
\fBqdbg-remote\fR or a DAP-compatible IDE.
.SS qdbg-vsc-adapter
Debug Adapter Protocol (DAP) implementation for Visual Studio Code.
Can launch programs locally or attach to a remote \fBqdbg-server\fR.
.SS qdbg-mcp
Model Context Protocol (MCP) server that lets coding agents debug Qore
programs: launch a script in its process or attach to a debug server, set
breakpoints, run until a thread pauses or a time passes, and read the call
stack, the variables and the values of expressions.
Agents connect to it with the HTTP transport of MCP.
.SH "QDBG OPTIONS"
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show help text and exit.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Increase verbosity (repeatable).
.TP
.BR \-D ", " \-\-define =\fIkey\fP[=\fIvalue\fP]
Set a parse define.
.TP
.BR \-p ", " \-\-set\-parse\-option =\fIoption\fP
Set a parse option (e.g., \fB\-pno\-database\fP).
.TP
.BR \-z ", " \-\-time\-zone =\fIzone\fP
Set the time zone.
.TP
.BR \-y ", " \-\-history =\fIfile\fP
Load command-line history from \fIfile\fP.
Use \fB.\fP to disable history.
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-\-session =\fIfile\fP
Load a saved debug session from \fIfile\fP.
.TP
.B \-\-color
Force color output.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-color
Disable color output.
.TP
.BR \-i ", " \-\-init\-file =\fIfile\fP
Run the commands of \fIfile\fP at the start instead of those of
\fI~/.qdbginit\fP.
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-no\-init
Do not run the commands of \fI~/.qdbginit\fP at the start.
.TP
.BR \-x ", " \-\-execute =\fIfile\fP
Run the commands of \fIfile\fP at the start, after those of the init file
(repeatable).
.TP
.B \-\-json
Write JSON Lines for programs such as coding agents: one object for each
command, event and output of the program; commands are read without a
prompt.
.TP
.BR \-\-wait\-timeout =\fIms\fP
The time that a command that resumes a thread waits for a thread to pause
when the input is not a terminal; then the program is paused.
.SH "QDBG-REMOTE OPTIONS"
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show help text and exit.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Increase verbosity (repeatable).
.TP
.BR \-m ", " \-\-max\-redir =\fIN\fP
Maximum number of HTTP redirects (default: 5).
.TP
.BR \-H ", " \-\-header =\fIkey=value\fP
Custom HTTP header for the connection (repeatable).
.TP
.BR \-P ", " \-\-proxy =\fIURL\fP
HTTP proxy URL.
.TP
.BR \-t ", " \-\-timeout =\fIms\fP
Connection timeout in milliseconds.
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-conn\-timeout =\fIms\fP
Socket connection timeout in milliseconds.
.TP
.BR \-w ", " \-\-resp\-timeout =\fIms\fP
WebSocket response timeout (default: 1500ms).
.TP
.BR \-y ", " \-\-history =\fIfile\fP
Load command-line history from \fIfile\fP.
Use \fB.\fP to disable history.
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-\-session =\fIfile\fP
Load a saved debug session from \fIfile\fP.
.TP
.B \-\-color
Force color output.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-color
Disable color output.
.TP
.BR \-i ", " \-\-init\-file =\fIfile\fP
Run the commands of \fIfile\fP at the start instead of those of
\fI~/.qdbginit\fP.
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-no\-init
Do not run the commands of \fI~/.qdbginit\fP at the start.
.TP
.BR \-x ", " \-\-execute =\fIfile\fP
Run the commands of \fIfile\fP at the start, after those of the init file
(repeatable).
.TP
.B \-\-json
Write JSON Lines for programs such as coding agents: one object for each
command, event and output of the program; commands are read without a
prompt.
.TP
.BR \-\-wait\-timeout =\fIms\fP
The time that a command that resumes a thread waits for a thread to pause
when the input is not a terminal; then the program is paused.
.SH "QDBG-SERVER OPTIONS"
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show help text and exit.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Increase verbosity (repeatable).
.TP
.BR \-l ", " \-\-listen =\fIaddr:port\fP
Listen address and port (repeatable).
Use a path starting with \fB/\fP for UNIX sockets.
Default: dynamic port.
.TP
.BR \-p ", " \-\-path =\fIpath\fP
URL path for the debug HTTP handler.
.SH "QDBG-VSC-ADAPTER OPTIONS"
.SS "Launch Options"
.TP
.BR \-D ", " \-\-define =\fIkey\fP[=\fIvalue\fP]
Set a parse define.
.TP
.BR \-p ", " \-\-set\-parse\-option =\fIoption\fP
Set a parse option for a launched program.
.TP
.BR \-z ", " \-\-time\-zone =\fIzone\fP
Set the time zone for a launched program.
.TP
.BR \-g ", " \-\-program =\fIprogram\fP
Use \fIprogram\fP unless a program is specified by the debug protocol.
.SS "Attach Options"
.TP
.BR \-a ", " \-\-attach =\fIurl\fP
Attach to a remote debug server.
.TP
.BR \-H ", " \-\-header =\fIkey=value\fP
Custom HTTP header for the connection (repeatable).
.TP
.BR \-m ", " \-\-max\-redir =\fIN\fP
Maximum number of HTTP redirects (default: 5).
.TP
.BR \-P ", " \-\-proxy =\fIURL\fP
HTTP proxy URL.
.TP
.BR \-t ", " \-\-timeout =\fIms\fP
Connection timeout in milliseconds.
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-conn\-timeout =\fIms\fP
Socket connection timeout in milliseconds.
.TP
.BR \-w ", " \-\-resp\-timeout =\fIms\fP
WebSocket response timeout.
.SS "Logging and General Options"
.TP
.BR \-l ", " \-\-logger\-filename =\fIfile\fP
Write adapter logs to \fIfile\fP.
.TP
.BR \-A ", " \-\-append\-to\-log
Append to the log file instead of replacing it.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Enable verbose logging.
.TP
.BR \-f ", " \-\-full\-exception
Show full exception information.
.TP
.BR \-X ", " \-\-execute =\fIcommand\fP
Execute an adapter command, print its result as JSON, and exit.
The supported command is \fBpgmlist\fP, which lists all programs.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show help text and exit.
.SH "QDBG-MCP OPTIONS"
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show help text and exit.
.TP
.BR \-l ", " \-\-listen =\fIaddress\fP
Listen on an address, such as \fB127.0.0.1:8100\fP or a UNIX socket path
(repeatable).
Default: a free port of 127.0.0.1.
.TP
.BR \-p ", " \-\-path =\fIpath\fP
The path of the MCP endpoint (default: \fBmcp\fP).
.TP
.BR \-k ", " \-\-token\-file =\fIfile\fP
Require the token in \fIfile\fP from the clients, sent as a bearer token;
the \fBQDBG_MCP_TOKEN\fP environment variable gives it too.
Required for an address that other hosts can reach.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-launch
Do not launch scripts in the process of the server; only attach to debug
servers.
.TP
.BR \-L ", " \-\-log\-file =\fIfile\fP
Write the log of the server to \fIfile\fP.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Log more details (repeatable).
.SH EXAMPLES
Debug a program locally:
.RS
.B qdbg \-v myprogram.q \-\-arg1 value
.RE
.PP
Run a script of debugger commands, without command history:
.RS
.B qdbg \-y . myprogram.q < commands
.RE
.PP
Run debugger commands from a program, with JSON output:
.RS
.B qdbg \-\-json \-\-wait\-timeout=5000 myprogram.q < commands
.RE
.PP
Let a coding agent debug Qore programs:
.RS
.B qdbg-mcp \-l 127.0.0.1:8100
.br
.B claude mcp add \-\-transport http qore-debug http://127.0.0.1:8100/mcp
.RE
.PP
Start a debug server:
.RS
.B qdbg-server \-l 127.0.0.1:10000 \-p debug myprogram.q
.RE
.PP
Connect to a remote debug server:
.RS
.B qdbg-remote localhost:10000/debug
.RE
